  "body": "Except in IE/Edge, if there is more than one value for accesskey then it will cause no accesskey to be assigned. (IE/Edge just take the first value and throw the rest away).\r\n\r\nSee the [W3C HTML spec where we clarified this](http://w3c.github.io/html/editing.html#the-accesskey-attribute), and https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/20 - note that in some browsers accesskeys which are more than one code point in length, but are produced with a single key, will work.",
